# SINPE Bridge - Environment Configuration


**Environment Variables**:
```
API_KEY=468bc1becd1b92ff7a6cdeafa31e891d
```

---

## FastAPI Backend

```bash
# .env file
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://user:pass@localhost/sinpe_bridge
DEBUG=False

API_KEY=<same-as-worker>
API_KEY_HEADER=x-api-key

MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE=104857600
REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30
SMS_CLOCK_SKEW_SECONDS=300

LOG_LEVEL=INFO
STRUCTURED_LOGGING=True

UPLOAD_STORAGE_PATH=/var/uploads

# Optional: Cloudflare R2
ENABLE_R2_STORAGE=False
R2_BUCKET_NAME=sinpe-bridge-uploads
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=<your-account-id>
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<access-key>
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=<secret-key>

# Features
ENABLE_OCR_PIPELINE=False
ENABLE_FRAUD_DETECTION=True
ENABLE_SMS_ARCHIVAL=True
```

**Requirements**:
```
fastapi==0.100.0
pydantic==2.5.0
pydantic-settings==2.0.0
sqlalchemy==2.0.23
psycopg[asyncio]==3.1.12
uvicorn==0.24.0
aiofiles==23.2.1
python-multipart==0.0.6
```

---

## Android App

```kotlin
// MainActivity or App.kt - in onCreate()
val httpConfig = HttpClientConfig(
    baseUrl = "https://api.tonyml.com",
    apiKey = "your-api-key-from-worker",
    timeoutSeconds = 30,
    enableLogging = BuildConfig.DEBUG,
)

SinpeBridgeHttpManager.initialize(context = this, config = httpConfig)
```

**Using HTTP Client**:
```kotlin
// SMS message
val result = SinpeBridgeHttpManager.getClient().postSmsMessage(
    smsBody = "SINPE 50000",
    sender = "1234567890",
    timestamp = System.currentTimeMillis() / 1000,
)

// Image upload
val uploadResult = SinpeBridgeHttpManager.getClient().uploadReceiptImage(
    filePath = "/path/to/image.jpg",
    imageType = "receipt_qr",
    messageId = null,
)
```

**Gradle Dependencies** (to add):
```gradle
dependencies {
    // OkHttp (already included via Ktor, but ensure latest)
    implementation "com.squareup.okhttp3:okhttp:4.12.0"
    
    // Async files
    implementation "androidx.work:work-runtime-ktx:2.9.0"  // For background uploads
}
```

